[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3219887341","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109955#issuecomment-3219887341","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109955","id":3219887341,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6_65Tt","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-25T11:24:30Z","updated_at":"2025-08-25T11:24:30Z","body":"Note, one option here is to split out the fix for OpenGL/Compatibility in a separate PR. That would be a nice and easy fix for Godot 4.5.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3219887341/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3226074222","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109955#issuecomment-3226074222","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109955","id":3226074222,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ASfxu","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-26T23:32:07Z","updated_at":"2025-08-26T23:32:07Z","body":"> Is the breaking change that `OpenXRInterface::get_color_texture()` will now return a rendering server texture RID, rather than a rendering device texture RID?\r\n> \r\n> If so, I actually think that makes more sense overall - it's always seemed a little weird to me that for OpenGL we return a rendering server texture RID, but not for Vulkan.\r\n\r\nYes, in hindsight it should have always worked this way. But changing it now, especially as we have some extensions doing things with swapchains, could cause issues.\r\n\r\nIt's possible the way I've done things hides the changes well enough that it will keep on working just fine (though there may be a few places I've missed).\r\n\r\nThe other part I'm not sure of is that this creates extra texture views and I don't know if that has any costs. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3226074222/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3226089779","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109955#issuecomment-3226089779","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109955","id":3226089779,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ASjkz","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-26T23:39:56Z","updated_at":"2025-08-26T23:39:56Z","body":"> I think we _may_ be able to prevent breaking binary compatibility for `XRInterfaceExtension` by having a virtual compatibility method that takes the rendering device texture and wraps it up in a rendering server texture? That would need some experimentation to see if it would work. (Not that there's many `XRInterfaceExtension`s in the wild - the main one being the OpenVR extension.)\r\n\r\nThings is, it's always just been RIDs we're pushing around so most of the extensions are none the wiser. Yes we now need to sent through `texture` RIDs instead of `texture_rd` RIDs, but as we now expose the `texture` RIDs through our swapchain wrapper class, that part should be transparent.\r\n\r\nThis is why it wasn't a problem that compatibility already used `texture` RIDs without causing any problems.\r\n\r\nHowever, if extensions perform additional actions here that assume we have a `texture_rd` RID that things fall a part. Or if I've forgotten some place that is still expecting `texture_rd` RIDs.  ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3226089779/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3226094570","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109955#issuecomment-3226094570","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109955","id":3226094570,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ASkvq","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-26T23:41:39Z","updated_at":"2025-08-26T23:41:39Z","body":"Btw @dsnopek , I'm probably going to split this PR in two, one purely for the changes to compatibility (seeing they are straight forward) and then changing this one to only handle the RendererRD changes. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3226094570/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3226663541","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109955#issuecomment-3226663541","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109955","id":3226663541,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7AUvp1","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-27T04:03:13Z","updated_at":"2025-08-27T04:03:13Z","body":"Extracted changes for compatibility renderer into https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110002\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3226663541/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3227235575","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109955#issuecomment-3227235575","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109955","id":3227235575,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7AW7T3","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-27T08:13:29Z","updated_at":"2025-08-27T08:13:29Z","body":"I added the functionality in for Metal and DX12 but this is as yet mostly untested so not ready for merging yet.\r\n\r\n@mbucchia I ran into a weird error on DX12 with this when we're attempting to create a slice on the textures. Do you mind having a quick test and see if I did something dumb or if we're missing something? ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3227235575/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3228331698","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109955#issuecomment-3228331698","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109955","id":3228331698,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7AbG6y","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-27T13:58:41Z","updated_at":"2025-08-27T13:58:41Z","body":"> > I think we _may_ be able to prevent breaking binary compatibility for `XRInterfaceExtension` by having a virtual compatibility method that takes the rendering device texture and wraps it up in a rendering server texture? That would need some experimentation to see if it would work. (Not that there's many `XRInterfaceExtension`s in the wild - the main one being the OpenVR extension.)\r\n> \r\n> Things is, it's always just been RIDs we're pushing around so most of the extensions are none the wiser. Yes we now need to sent through `texture` RIDs instead of `texture_rd` RIDs, but as we now expose the `texture` RIDs through our swapchain wrapper class, that part should be transparent.\r\n\r\nActually, my idea with using a compatibility method won't work, because the method hash won't change. But I still think we could potentially come up with a way to minimize the compatibility breakage.\r\n\r\nSomething like (untested):\r\n\r\n```c++\r\nRID XRInterfaceExtension::get_color_texture() {\r\n\tRID texture;\r\n\tGDVIRTUAL_CALL(_get_color_texture, texture);\r\n\r\n#ifndef DISABLE_DEPRECATED\r\n\tRenderingDevice *rd = RenderingDevice::get_singleton();\r\n\tif (texture.is_valid()  && rd) {\r\n\t\t// @todo We should cache the RS texture that is made, and not remake it if we get the same RD texture\t\r\n\t\tif (rd->texture_is_valid(texture)) {\r\n\t\t\tRID texture_rd = texture;\r\n\t\t\ttexture = texture_storage->texture_allocate();\r\n\t\t\ttexture_storage->texture_rd_initialize(texture, texture_rd);\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n#endif\r\n\treturn texture;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut, yeah, it's certainly possible that an extension is doing something advanced that could break. However, if we can test all the GDExtensions we're aware of, and it works, we'll probably have covered 99% of possible use cases.\r\n\r\nFYI, I took a quick peek at [godot_openvr](https://github.com/GodotVR/godot_openvr), [godot_arcore](https://github.com/GodotVR/godot_arcore) and [TiltFiveGodot4](https://github.com/GodotVR/TiltFiveGodot4). I don't think godot_openvr or godot_arcore will be affected at all - they appear not to be using the texture override stuff, but the blits returned by `_post_draw_viewport()`. TiltFiveGodot4 does use the texture overrides, but I suspect it would be OK - would need some testing.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3228331698/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3232002450","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109955#issuecomment-3232002450","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109955","id":3232002450,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ApHGS","user":{"login":"mbucchia","id":69611560,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NjExNTYw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69611560?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia","html_url":"https://github.com/mbucchia","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mbucchia/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-28T05:56:59Z","updated_at":"2025-08-28T05:59:53Z","body":"> @mbucchia I ran into a weird error on DX12 with this when we're attempting to create a slice on the textures. Do you mind having a quick test and see if I did something dumb or if we're missing something?\r\n\r\nAny specific repro steps? Just the xr template?\r\nEdit: Do I use the \"spectator demo\" on the linked issue?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3232002450/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3232505229","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109955#issuecomment-3232505229","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109955","id":3232505229,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ArB2N","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-28T08:35:48Z","updated_at":"2025-08-28T08:35:48Z","body":"@dsnopek the problem is that we don't have a proper lifecycle for the created texture object. It should be freed when the RD texture is freed but... That said, I like the general idea of your fix, checking if the RID is RD texture RID and if so, wrapping it in a texture RD object.. Yeah...\r\n\r\n@mbucchia yeah just test with the spectator demo: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/pull/1144\r\nI'm going to give it another try myself, the more I think about it, the more convinced I am I just made a mistake somewhere.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3232505229/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3233181449","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109955#issuecomment-3233181449","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109955","id":3233181449,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Atm8J","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-28T11:49:53Z","updated_at":"2025-08-28T11:49:53Z","body":"@mbucchia I've chased the value to this point in the code: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/drivers/d3d12/rendering_device_driver_d3d12.cpp#L1491\r\n```\r\nRDD::TextureID RenderingDeviceDriverD3D12::_texture_create_shared_from_slice(TextureID p_original_texture, const TextureView &p_view, TextureSliceType p_slice_type, uint32_t p_layer, uint32_t p_layers, uint32_t p_mipmap, uint32_t p_mipmaps) {\r\n\tTextureInfo *owner_tex_info = (TextureInfo *)p_original_texture.id;\r\n#ifdef DEBUG_ENABLED\r\n\tERR_FAIL_COND_V(!owner_tex_info->owner_info.allocation, TextureID());\r\n#endif\r\n```\r\n\r\nI think because this texture is created within OpenXR and we use `texture_create_from_extension` to then create our texture structure around it, we don't have information about it's creation. \r\nThis is a little beyond me to know whether we can solve this differently and make `_texture_create_shared_from_slice` work with a texture that's been created from outside our sphere of influence.\r\nI'm actually surprised we haven't run into this yet because we create a number of slices on this texture. There must be something different in what we're adding here compared to what we're doing elsewhere when rendering a frame.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3233181449/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]